WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:02.010
- I have Justin Timberlake
and Anna Kendrick

00:00:02.010 --> 00:00:02.843
with me on Zoom.

00:00:02.843 --> 00:00:04.240
My first Zoom interview.

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:07.710
And anyway, the cool thing
about talking remotely

00:00:07.710 --> 00:00:09.530
is we get to see people's homes,

00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:11.910
and we get to kind of peer
into their quarantine lives.

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:14.820
So I know a lot of
people are playing games

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:16.390
or doing puzzles and all those things.

00:00:16.390 --> 00:00:19.340
So I thought that we
would do a game as well.

00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:21.980
And I know how much celebrities
just love doing games

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:24.420
on shows, so I thought you would, too.

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:27.470
So (laughs), we're gonna do a game called

00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:28.839
Zoom around the Room.

00:00:28.839 --> 00:00:30.130
(game show music)

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:31.250
Here's how it goes.

00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:33.030
We'll be given, by my producer

00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:36.900
we'll be given a word or a
phrase, and we will each run

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:40.100
to find the object that matches that word.

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:42.610
First person, I see, okay I
thought Justin was stretching.

00:00:42.610 --> 00:00:44.100
I thought, man, he's
really getting into this

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:45.220
but he's (laughs)
- No, I'm looking.

00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:48.100
I'm like, whoa, okay,
okay, taking inventory.

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:50.390
- You look like, you're like
in a padded, white room,

00:00:50.390 --> 00:00:53.680
so good luck finding stuff. (laughs)

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:55.560
The first person back to the camera

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:58.590
with the item gets the point, okay?

00:00:58.590 --> 00:01:00.880
So they're gonna type in something.

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:02.400
I'm gonna read it off.

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:04.900
I don't know either, so
we're just gonna grab stuff.

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:05.950
And then whoever's back gets a point.

00:01:05.950 --> 00:01:08.470
And then you need to explain
why you pulled that thing.

00:01:08.470 --> 00:01:09.380
Are you ready?

00:01:09.380 --> 00:01:10.440
- Yes.

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:11.273
- Okay.

00:01:11.273 --> 00:01:12.106
- Zoom around the room.

00:01:12.106 --> 00:01:15.663
Okay, so Alex, why don't
you give us the first clue?

00:01:15.663 --> 00:01:19.171
Okay, so go find something red!

00:01:19.171 --> 00:01:20.228
- Okay.
- [Kelly] Something red!

00:01:20.228 --> 00:01:21.743
(timer ticking)

00:01:21.743 --> 00:01:23.575
Oh my god! Oh wait! (laughs)

00:01:23.575 --> 00:01:26.160
(timer ticking)

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:27.463
I killed y'all.

00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:30.040
- I'm not gonna be fast, guys.

00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:31.040
I'm not gonna be fast.

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:32.513
- I killed y'all!

00:01:33.716 --> 00:01:36.280
Okay, I'm gonna try to
walk slower for you.

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:37.600
I'm in a small cabin, y'all.

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:38.660
There's not many places to hide stuff.

00:01:38.660 --> 00:01:39.850
- I don't like the color red that much.

00:01:39.850 --> 00:01:41.210
And I don't have much red.

00:01:41.210 --> 00:01:43.657
- What?! Who doesn't like the color red?!

00:01:44.970 --> 00:01:46.508
We're gonna have to talk about that later.

00:01:46.508 --> 00:01:47.341
- Okay.

00:01:47.341 --> 00:01:49.480
- I definitely had this urge to be like

00:01:51.283 --> 00:01:52.700
(laughter)

00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:54.749
- Look what's funny, this is mine!

00:01:54.749 --> 00:01:55.582
(laughter)

00:01:55.582 --> 00:01:57.123
We're so in Montana.

00:01:57.123 --> 00:01:59.960
(laughter)

00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:01.590
Okay, go ahead, Anna, and explain yours.

00:02:01.590 --> 00:02:02.810
What is that?

00:02:02.810 --> 00:02:04.593
- This is a can of wine.

00:02:05.566 --> 00:02:07.810
(laughter)

00:02:07.810 --> 00:02:08.920
Hi.

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:11.440
- Next time, I'm quarentining
with you. (laughs)

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:14.580
- Yeah, I mean, the sun is
out, so what are we doing?

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:16.190
- Did you say a can of wine?

00:02:16.190 --> 00:02:18.790
Very fancy, and maybe a nice...

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:21.460
- It's a all-day, right?

00:02:21.460 --> 00:02:23.152
- Yeah. (laughs)

00:02:23.152 --> 00:02:24.350
- And it's red, so I'm good.

00:02:24.350 --> 00:02:28.050
- Okay, so what is yours,
Justin, other than your shirt?

00:02:28.050 --> 00:02:30.300
- This is a mixing bowl from this morning.

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:34.140
I was talking about those
banana chocolate chip muffins.

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:35.890
- Okay, I'm actually in the room

00:02:35.890 --> 00:02:37.950
where I happen to quilt and do crafts.

00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:39.580
So, I'm a quilter.

00:02:39.580 --> 00:02:40.980
So this is um...

00:02:40.980 --> 00:02:42.530
I know, it's like, once
you have kids it's like,

00:02:42.530 --> 00:02:44.610
I'm gonna do these motherly things.

00:02:44.610 --> 00:02:47.210
And then, whatever, I don't
know, you become weird.

00:02:47.210 --> 00:02:48.560
But anyway, so I have that.

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:50.200
That's, like, one of the pieces I use.

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:52.050
Okay, next clue!

00:02:52.050 --> 00:02:52.900
Kelly gets first point.

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:53.890
Yes!

00:02:53.890 --> 00:02:56.137
Find something from your childhood?!

00:02:57.050 --> 00:02:57.883
What?

00:02:57.883 --> 00:02:58.787
- Find something from your childhood?

00:02:58.787 --> 00:03:00.237
- Find something from your childhood!

00:03:00.237 --> 00:03:01.263
- Oh, gosh.

00:03:05.872 --> 00:03:06.810
- Whoo!

00:03:06.810 --> 00:03:07.940
I got something.

00:03:07.940 --> 00:03:10.160
Oh my god, did I win again?!

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:11.220
- [Justin] I don't have anything.

00:03:11.220 --> 00:03:13.370
Something from my childhood?

00:03:13.370 --> 00:03:15.420
- Fun fact, I wore that veil as a shaw

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:18.014
to the Tony Awards when
I was 12-years-old.

00:03:18.014 --> 00:03:20.020
- (gasps) When you were how old?

00:03:20.020 --> 00:03:20.853
- 12-years-old.

00:03:20.853 --> 00:03:22.040
- Wait, what?

00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:23.050
Wait, I missed something.

00:03:23.050 --> 00:03:25.563
You went to the Tony
Awards at 12-years-old?

00:03:26.460 --> 00:03:27.450
- I was nominated!

00:03:27.450 --> 00:03:28.730
Did you not know? (laughs)

00:03:28.730 --> 00:03:30.340
- At 12-years-old?!

00:03:30.340 --> 00:03:31.320
- Yeah.

00:03:31.320 --> 00:03:32.310
- [Justin] What did I miss?
- [Kelly] Holy Crap!

00:03:32.310 --> 00:03:33.810
- Yeah, like what?

00:03:33.810 --> 00:03:35.140
- Nobody told me that.

00:03:35.140 --> 00:03:36.830
I did not know that, Anna!

00:03:36.830 --> 00:03:38.570
- It's weird. (laughs)
- That's incredible!

00:03:38.570 --> 00:03:40.140
- I know, it's weird.

00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:41.130
- What were you in?

00:03:41.130 --> 00:03:43.010
What did you do?

00:03:43.010 --> 00:03:45.820
- I was in the musical "High Society,"

00:03:45.820 --> 00:03:47.840
which is based on the,
like, Grace Kelly movie.

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:50.090
Which is based on the musical.
- I knew "High Society!"

00:03:50.090 --> 00:03:51.823
I didn't know that.

00:03:51.823 --> 00:03:53.400
That is so cool.

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:54.900
- It's so wild.

00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:56.980
Like, sometimes I'm like, what?

00:03:56.980 --> 00:03:59.240
- Learning something new on Zoom, okay.

00:03:59.240 --> 00:04:01.230
Okay, what did you find
from your childhood?

00:04:01.230 --> 00:04:04.680
(laughs) What is that?

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:06.700
- There was just some old,
there was just some old,

00:04:06.700 --> 00:04:09.320
you know the old, just letters

00:04:09.320 --> 00:04:11.620
where you're teaching your kids to spell.

00:04:11.620 --> 00:04:15.530
This is one that I had
that we brought up here.

00:04:15.530 --> 00:04:19.283
I picked a K, just for
"Kelly" and "Kendrick."

00:04:19.283 --> 00:04:21.390
- Good job!

00:04:21.390 --> 00:04:23.330
Totally for bookpile, right?
- This is one

00:04:23.330 --> 00:04:26.403
that's been passed on to my little guy.

00:04:27.290 --> 00:04:29.177
It's the K in "Timberlake."

00:04:30.079 --> 00:04:31.550
- You are so full of crap right now,

00:04:31.550 --> 00:04:32.450
but I'm okay with it.

00:04:32.450 --> 00:04:33.283
- No, no, no!

00:04:33.283 --> 00:04:34.893
This is true, this is true, this is--

00:04:34.893 --> 00:04:35.726
- That is?!

00:04:35.726 --> 00:04:37.040
I thought you just grabbed
a toy from your kid

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:38.467
and were like, "Yeah, this was passed down

00:04:38.467 --> 00:04:41.170
from my great grandmother."

00:04:41.170 --> 00:04:42.417
- No, no, no.

00:04:42.417 --> 00:04:45.300
This shows you I'm not
willing to spend money

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:46.740
on new toys for my children.

00:04:46.740 --> 00:04:48.180
I just passed down.

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:49.013
- That's adorable!

00:04:49.013 --> 00:04:51.500
It's passed down that much,
like, really cool! (laughs)

00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:54.940
- Yeah, there are all these,
just to, you know, spelling.

00:04:54.940 --> 00:04:55.807
Here's your letters.
- Okay, this is,

00:04:55.807 --> 00:04:59.110
I made sure to bring this with me

00:04:59.110 --> 00:05:00.793
because I love NES.
- Oh, wow!

00:05:03.100 --> 00:05:05.470
- Yes, and I'm just
gonna be honest with you.

00:05:05.470 --> 00:05:06.960
They have the new one, where it came out,

00:05:06.960 --> 00:05:08.640
and you got all the
games from your childhood

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:10.950
like, on this, because we're
all around the same age.

00:05:10.950 --> 00:05:13.500
Anyway, I'm not gonna lie.

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:16.730
If you played me at Mario-anything,

00:05:16.730 --> 00:05:19.230
I would make you feel
so bad about yourself

00:05:19.230 --> 00:05:21.590
'cause I'm so talented at it.

00:05:21.590 --> 00:05:22.693
I'm so good.

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:24.663
I'm just saying.

00:05:25.750 --> 00:05:27.323
Did you play Mario Brothers?

00:05:28.740 --> 00:05:30.720
I will crush anyone I'm playing.

00:05:30.720 --> 00:05:32.240
My husband, it's sad.

00:05:32.240 --> 00:05:33.073
He just drinks.

00:05:34.370 --> 00:05:38.140
- Does that Nintendo come with Excitebike?

00:05:38.140 --> 00:05:39.270
- Yes!

00:05:39.270 --> 00:05:40.103
- It does?

00:05:40.103 --> 00:05:42.457
- Oh my gosh, with the hill, yes!

00:05:42.457 --> 00:05:43.960
- That was, damn.

00:05:43.960 --> 00:05:47.170
I remember when you
bought the first Nintendo,

00:05:47.170 --> 00:05:49.630
it would come with, like, Mario Brothers

00:05:49.630 --> 00:05:51.270
and then--
- Duck Hunt.

00:05:51.270 --> 00:05:54.210
- Yeah, Duck Hunt, and
then, I think, Excitebike.

00:05:54.210 --> 00:05:56.056
Or, maybe (audio cuts out).

00:05:56.056 --> 00:05:56.889
I don't know.

00:05:56.889 --> 00:05:57.740
- No, that was awesome.

00:05:57.740 --> 00:06:00.400
Yeah, anyway, I love playing this

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:04.223
while inebriated, just gonna
say inebriated, yeah. (laughs)

00:06:05.520 --> 00:06:10.420
- No this, you know,
drinking, let's all be real.

00:06:10.420 --> 00:06:11.253
It's happening.

00:06:11.253 --> 00:06:12.086
It's happening.

00:06:12.086 --> 00:06:14.122
- It's happening right now. (laughs)

00:06:14.122 --> 00:06:15.260
- Yeah.

00:06:15.260 --> 00:06:18.480
Anyway, okay, so, this is the last one

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:21.260
because I'm long-winded,
and you're welcome, team.

00:06:21.260 --> 00:06:23.900
Anyway, we have to find
something related to you.

00:06:23.900 --> 00:06:25.934
Okay, find related--
- What does that mean?

00:06:25.934 --> 00:06:26.767
What does that mean?

00:06:26.767 --> 00:06:27.780
- What does that mean?

00:06:27.780 --> 00:06:28.669
- What does that mean?

00:06:28.669 --> 00:06:30.018
- [Kelly] Metaphorically or physical.

00:06:30.018 --> 00:06:32.270
(timer ticking)

00:06:32.270 --> 00:06:33.513
- Wait, wait, wait.

00:06:38.090 --> 00:06:39.679
Does this count as related to me?

00:06:39.679 --> 00:06:40.512
- Boom.

00:06:40.512 --> 00:06:43.920
- Oh, look at what we just did! (laughs)

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:45.643
I stole my kid's toy.

00:06:48.820 --> 00:06:49.980
- I got one better than that.

00:06:49.980 --> 00:06:51.765
I stole my kid. (laughs)

00:06:51.765 --> 00:06:53.353
- Awwwww!

00:06:53.353 --> 00:06:55.183
- This is River.
- Aw, Kelly wins again.

00:06:55.183 --> 00:06:56.360
Hi!

00:06:56.360 --> 00:06:57.820
- Oh, hey, come here!

00:06:57.820 --> 00:07:00.210
They were about to head
out with our niece.

00:07:00.210 --> 00:07:01.550
So come here!

00:07:01.550 --> 00:07:03.370
This is Remi.

00:07:03.370 --> 00:07:04.620
We were just watching Trolls.

00:07:04.620 --> 00:07:06.183
So this is Branch, and this is Poppy.

00:07:06.183 --> 00:07:07.277
- Hi.

00:07:07.277 --> 00:07:08.110
- Hi!

00:07:08.110 --> 00:07:08.943
- Can you say hi?

00:07:08.943 --> 00:07:09.776
- Hi.

00:07:12.981 --> 00:07:13.980
- You did your hair, man?

00:07:13.980 --> 00:07:14.813
Okay.

00:07:14.813 --> 00:07:17.370
Somebody thought they
were gonna be on camera.

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:18.950
Hey, can you say bye to them?

00:07:18.950 --> 00:07:19.790
- Byyyeee!

00:07:19.790 --> 00:07:22.110
- Do you like Trolls?
- Bye!

00:07:22.110 --> 00:07:23.290
- You love Trolls.

00:07:23.290 --> 00:07:25.910
- And I loved your acting.

00:07:25.910 --> 00:07:28.544
I love Poppy and Bridgette.

00:07:28.544 --> 00:07:29.915
- (laughs) And Branch.

00:07:29.915 --> 00:07:31.267
- (audio cuts out)
- Oh my god.

00:07:33.033 --> 00:07:34.590
- Aright, were you kind of worried

00:07:34.590 --> 00:07:36.880
that mommy was gonna be a mean troll?

00:07:36.880 --> 00:07:37.880
Yeah?
- [River] No.

00:07:39.162 --> 00:07:41.270
Look at her face!

00:07:41.270 --> 00:07:44.830
Alright, so, sorry,
something related to you.

00:07:44.830 --> 00:07:46.793
What did you get, Anna?

00:07:46.793 --> 00:07:47.626
- I got Poppy.

00:07:47.626 --> 00:07:49.947
- Oh my god, you both! (laughs)

00:07:49.947 --> 00:07:51.930
- Well I was, it was related to me!

00:07:51.930 --> 00:07:53.770
Nobody's in the house.

00:07:53.770 --> 00:07:54.603
- That's awesome.

00:07:54.603 --> 00:07:55.630
That's related to you.

00:07:55.630 --> 00:07:56.800
There you go.

00:07:56.800 --> 00:07:57.633
This was perfect.

00:07:57.633 --> 00:07:58.710
That's amazing.

00:07:58.710 --> 00:07:59.820
Okay, cool.

00:07:59.820 --> 00:08:02.390
Alright, well the winner
is, was there a doubt?

00:08:02.390 --> 00:08:03.770
It's me, yep.

00:08:03.770 --> 00:08:04.920
Anna, you came in second.

00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:07.450
But, you know, if you're
not first, you're last.

00:08:07.450 --> 00:08:08.980
Thank y'all for doing this.

00:08:08.980 --> 00:08:11.030
It's entertaining to
people that are at home

00:08:11.030 --> 00:08:13.460
and don't have anything, you know, to do.

00:08:13.460 --> 00:08:15.150
And they're bored, and
so, thank you so much

00:08:15.150 --> 00:08:16.083
for just taking the time, 'cause I know

00:08:16.083 --> 00:08:17.890
that all of us are going
through it as well,

00:08:17.890 --> 00:08:19.490
so sometimes, it sucks, you have to smile

00:08:19.490 --> 00:08:20.590
and be like, "It's gonna be great!"

00:08:20.590 --> 00:08:22.840
Even though in your head,
you're like, "It might not be."

00:08:22.840 --> 00:08:24.710
- I'm just gonna have a little cry

00:08:24.710 --> 00:08:26.890
and then go back to saying that
everything's gonna be great.

00:08:26.890 --> 00:08:28.300
- Yeah (laughs).

00:08:28.300 --> 00:08:30.140
Anyway--
- It's gonna be okay!

00:08:30.140 --> 00:08:31.950
- I am glad that you're safe in Montana

00:08:31.950 --> 00:08:32.890
and staying healthy.

00:08:32.890 --> 00:08:34.590
Justin, say hi to your family for us.

00:08:34.590 --> 00:08:36.940
Glad you just had a birthday
party with your kiddos, Alex.

00:08:36.940 --> 00:08:38.880
And Anna, thank you so much for coming on

00:08:38.880 --> 00:08:42.020
and looking, just, fabulous,
and if I'm in quarantine,

00:08:42.020 --> 00:08:43.610
next time, I want you to be with me.

00:08:43.610 --> 00:08:46.450
So that you can do my
hair and makeup. (laughs)

00:08:46.450 --> 00:08:48.400
All right, well, I love you guys,

00:08:48.400 --> 00:08:50.310
and I'll just see y'all next time

00:08:50.310 --> 00:08:52.078
maybe in person, how about that?

00:08:52.078 --> 00:08:52.911
- (laughs) Yes.

00:08:52.911 --> 00:08:55.937
- [Justin] Yeah, I would
love that, I would love that.

